From 20775d8af221fad2ebc896147996da4bfaf3ccbb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: silo-research <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 14:06:30 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 09/10] gvproxy: add -outbound-handoff

Some users want every connection of the guest decided, logged or
rewritten by a program of theirs before it reaches the network: an
egress proxy with an allow list by name, a recorder, a program that
injects credentials the guest must not hold. Today they have to run
that program as a transparent proxy behind gvproxy on the host, which
needs root, or set proxy variables in the guest, which programs are free
to ignore.

-outbound-handoff <path>, or `stack.outboundHandoff`, hands every TCP
connection of the guest to the unix socket at path, after a PROXY
protocol v2 header with the guest's address and port and the
destination after NAT translation, and gvproxy dials nothing itself.
PROXY v2 is read by HAProxy, Envoy, nginx and common libraries, so the
program needs no format of gvproxy's. Outbound UDP and ICMP are dropped,
since only a stream can be handed over and nothing else may leave. If
nothing listens on the socket, the guest's connection is reset.

The dial filter, the deny list and the link-local rule still apply
before the hand-off. It uses Configuration.DialTCP, and cannot be set
together with it.
