diff --git a/README.md b/README.md
index 82bf35b9..bf545631 100644
--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -220,6 +220,16 @@ For example, `--outbound-deny private,host,host-networks` lets the VM reach the
 the host nor its local network. It is checked on the address gvproxy dials, after NAT, so
 192.168.127.254 is refused through its loopback target. Forwards into the VM are not affected.
 
+### Handing connections to a proxy
+
+`--outbound-handoff /path/to/socket` makes gvproxy open no outbound connection itself. Each TCP
+connection of the VM is handed to that unix socket, preceded by a
+[PROXY protocol v2](https://www.haproxy.org/download/3.0/doc/proxy-protocol.txt) header that
+carries the VM's address and the destination it asked for (after NAT). The program listening
+there, a proxy that HAProxy, Envoy, nginx or Go's `go-proxyproto` can be, decides and opens the
+connection. Outbound UDP and pings are dropped. If nothing listens, the VM's connections are reset.
+Combine it with `--dns-upstream` to have the same program answer the VM's lookups.
+
 ### DNS
 
 The gateway also runs a DNS server. It can be configured to serve static zones.
